  {
   "id": "n1",
   "scene": "recap",
   "text": "Did you feel that journey? You were a male Aedes mosquito with Wolbachia inside. You were released at an HDB block. Males don't bite, so you just flew around, looking for a female. You found one and mated with her. But her eggs could not hatch. So, fewer mosquitoes, and less dengue.",
   "hold": 1.0
  },
  {
   "id": "textbook",
   "scene": "textbook",
   "text": "Now for the textbook link! In Primary Three, you learn about life cycles. A mosquito's life cycle has four stages: egg, larva, pupa and adult. The first three stages happen in water. That's why we never leave water standing in flower pot plates!",
